# A safety net under the Dockerfile's allowlist (#386, #397): the runtime
# stage copies only named files and directories, and the test stage adds
# tests/ and cli/. This list keeps secrets and local state out even when
# they sit inside a copied directory; anything left in an image's layers
# can be read by whoever pulls it (#163). The CI build job plants a decoy
# for each secret/state pattern (its DECOYS list) and fails if one leaks
# into either image: add new patterns to both.

# Secrets and local state
# .env.example holds only placeholders, and the tests load it.
**/.env*
!.env.example
**/*.db*
**/*.sqlite3
**/db.json
data/
uploads/
instance/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
# Playwright reports and traces record typed passwords and session cookies.
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Development clutter
.git/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
coverage/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
**/.DS_Store
